@startuml
title Figure 2. ResourceHive Container and Service Architecture
left to right direction
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 65
skinparam shadowing false
actor User
rectangle "Frontend Hosting" {
  component "Next.js Web Application" as Web
}
node "Docker-capable Backend Host" {
  component "Nginx API Gateway" as Gateway
  component "Identity Service\nNestJS" as Identity
  component "Resource Service\nNestJS" as Resource
  component "Booking Service\nNestJS" as Booking
  component "Notification Service\nNestJS" as Notification
  component "Shared service-auth package" as AuthPkg
  component "Shared Prisma database package" as DbPkg
}
database "Shared PostgreSQL" as DB
cloud "SMTP / OAuth Providers" as Providers
User --> Web : HTTPS
Web --> Gateway : HTTPS/JSON + JWT cookie/header
Gateway --> Identity : /auth
Gateway --> Resource : /organizations\n/memberships\n/resources
Gateway --> Booking : /slots\n/bookings\n/points\n/disputes
Gateway --> Notification : /notifications
Identity ..> AuthPkg
Resource ..> AuthPkg
Booking ..> AuthPkg
Notification ..> AuthPkg
Identity ..> DbPkg
Resource ..> DbPkg
Booking ..> DbPkg
Notification ..> DbPkg
DbPkg --> DB : Prisma/SQL
Identity --> Providers : Email and OAuth
Notification --> Providers : Delivery adapter
note bottom of Gateway
Routing and transport only;
no tenant authorization logic.
end note
@enduml


